  nonce: fbd4  # fbd4
  message: "Fixed (PR merged as d79bc37f45). Root cause (pinned by adversarial workflow wf_159e8b4a): the WRITE path (run_behavior_map with out_path=None, cli.py:8888-8891) and the READ path (_discover_input_file, cli.py:434) call the IDENTICAL helper _get_results_cache_dir(repo_root) = <cache_base>/<fingerprint>/results/<state_hash>/<analyzer_identity>/hypergumbo.results.json, so the paths are structurally byte-identical — my earlier 'path mismatch' framing was WRONG. The real defect: _get_results_cache_dir is NOT idempotent across the analysis window because segment #3 <state_hash> = _get_repo_state_hash(repo_root) = compute_repo_fingerprint(repo_root)[:16] is a LIVE content hash of the git-dirty file set (git HEAD + hashed contents of every dirty/untracked-non-ignored file). run_behavior_map computes it at its START to pick the WRITE dir; _get_or_run_analysis then RE-computed it AFTER the multi-second run (via the second _discover_input_file call) to pick the READ dir. In the self-analysis + smart-test scenario the repo's dirty content changes mid-run (concurrent tracker .ops / .ci writes), so the recomputed <state_hash> drifts, the READ stats a directory the WRITE never populated, _discover_input_file returns None (the cli.py:527 '# pragma: no cover - shouldnt happen' branch FIRED in prod), and cmd_slice printed 'Error: Input file not found: None' -> smart-test full-suite-fell-back to a pre-commit-rejected manifest. FIX (structural, drift-immune): _get_or_run_analysis now returns the map run_behavior_map ACTUALLY wrote — out_path is unconditionally appended to generated_files at cli.py:9566 — selected BY NAME (p.name == 'hypergumbo.results.json') so a budget side-output (hypergumbo.results.<tier>.json) or a handler-slice file is never returned instead. The re-discovery (and its state_hash recomputation) is eliminated from the post-run path; the pre-run warm-cache read keeps using _discover_input_file (no drift window there). Adversarially verified SAFE on the other four _get_or_run_analysis paths: explicit_input (returns early), warm-cache-hit (returns before running), side-outputs-in-generated_files (name filter excludes them), non-directory SubstrateError (raised before the edited block). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: (1) production-path unit test test_cli_run_behavior_map.py::test_get_or_run_analysis_returns_generated_main_map_on_cold_cache drives the real _get_or_run_analysis cold-cache branch — a fake run writes the map to a dir _discover_input_file never checks and returns it (main map NOT last, proving name-not-positional select); the fn now returns that path where it returned None before (RED->GREEN). (2) LIVE END-TO-END: with the repo-root discovery-fallback workaround REMOVED (forcing the real cold-cache path that failed in the bundle-6 run), 'BASE_BRANCH=selfh/dev pytest' produced a '# Mode: targeted' manifest via a cold-cache 'hypergumbo slice --files' — the exact command that emitted 'Input file not found: None' and forced a full-suite fallback before this fix. The cli.py:527 pragma is KEPT as an honest defensive guard (run_behavior_map always appends the main map). 100% coverage. (Note: the stale-analysis-cache observation from the WI-mulub census — cross_language/dest_access_mode/construct lingering in cached self-maps — is a DISTINCT cache-correctness concern, not addressed here.)"  # fbd4
